Q: How to change iFrame src with a default value when the original src does not exist? A: <p>Something like this should work:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;html&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;input id=&quot;year&quot; type=&quot;number&quot; min=&quot;2000&quot; max=&quot;2099&quot; value=&quot;2025&quot; onchange=&quot;getContent(this.value)&quot;/&gt;
  &lt;br&gt;
  &lt;iframe id=&quot;content&quot; name=&quot;content&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
  &lt;script&gt;
    async function getContent(year) {
        var iframe = document.getElementById('content');
        try {
            let result = await fetch('./' + year + '.html')
            iframe.src = year + &quot;.html&quot;;
        } catch (error) {
            iframe.src = &quot;Empty.html&quot;;
        }
    }
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>If we attempt a fetch first within a <code>try/catch</code>, then default the iFrame's src to <code>Empty.html</code> if we fail.</p>
